  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1143 AM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nAs the cold front sweeps out of the area Thursday night taking rain \nchances with it, crisp autumn weather takes over on blustery north \nwinds and much drier air. Low stratus initially in the post-frontal \nlayer will scour out on Friday, but skies will be partly to mostly \ncloudy under a stubborn plume of high clouds. Even without the high \nclouds, high temps look capped in the 50s which sets the stage for a \nchilly night as the high clouds clear and north winds go calm. \nLatest MOS and NBM probs are trending colder everywhere with a light \nfreeze not out of the question for much of the Caprock, which is 1-2 \nweeks ahead of schedule for many locales. High temps remain below\nnormal through the weekend under weak upper ridging before slowly\nrecovering next week ahead of the next slow-moving upper low that\nis favored to direct another plume of subtropical moisture our \nway. Rain chances gear up by mid week and continue thereafter with\nnear normal temps.",
